1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,260
In Mario Kart 8,

2
00:00:01,260 --> 00:00:04,480
a collision can become a chance to accelerate.

3
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,660
The condition is an anti-gravity section.

4
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:08,820
Where you collide, and with what, both matter.

5
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:11,440
Not every collision gives a speed boost.

6
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:13,180
First identify the section where the wheels turn sideways

7
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:15,380
and the kart hovers.

8
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:17,660
The reward for contact depends

9
00:00:17,660 --> 00:00:19,480
on the kart’s driving state.

10
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:20,520
In anti-gravity sections,

11
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:22,980
racers can drive on walls or upside-down roads.

12
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:24,780
The road’s orientation is not the only change:

13
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:26,960
the meaning of contact changes too.

14
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:28,640
Another kart you would normally avoid

15
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:30,940
can become something useful here.

16
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:32,140
When the road turns onto a wall,

17
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:34,880
you begin looking for more than things to avoid.

18
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:36,720
You also look for contact opportunities

19
00:00:36,720 --> 00:00:38,160
that can send you forward.

20
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:40,160
Nintendo introduced a move where, in anti-gravity,

21
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:41,700
colliding with another kart

22
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:45,080
makes you spin and gain speed: Spin Turbo.

23
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:46,720
Moving closer to another racer

24
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,240
now offers a reward.

25
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:49,180
Remember that this explanation

26
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:52,000
is conditional on anti-gravity mode.

27
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,400
In an anti-gravity section, contact with another kart

28
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:56,800
can trigger a spin and speed boost.

29
00:00:56,800 --> 00:00:59,460
That reward creates a choice to approach,

30
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:02,120
instead of avoiding every contact.

31
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:05,140
Certain obstacles offer the same opportunity.

32
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:07,460
“Certain” is important here.

33
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:09,440
Every wall and decoration

34
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:12,120
should not be treated as a boost device.

35
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:14,340
Identify objects that actually give this effect

36
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:15,920
and plan your route around them.

37
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:18,040
Here, watch the kart spin

38
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:20,660
immediately after contacting the glowing post.

39
00:01:20,660 --> 00:01:22,140
That does not turn every ordinary wall nearby

40
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,760
into the same boost device.

41
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:28,460
Anti-gravity, eligible contact, a spinning boost.

42
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:29,500
With those conditions combined,

43
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:32,640
a collision becomes a choice, rather than just a mistake.

44
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:34,980
Along with twisting the road, Mario Kart 8

45
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:37,640
changes why you might approach another racer.

46
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,860
The rule turns some contact

47
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,180
from a penalty into a speed opportunity.

48
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:43,720
In an anti-gravity section,

49
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:46,660
other racers and devices become part of route choice.

50
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:47,760
The new driving space

51
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:49,680
also gains a new kind of interaction.
